Input: {"question": "Which feature does Klockgjutargränd end at?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 96, "text": "Title: The Hidden Corners of Gamla Stan: Unveiling the Secrets of Klockgjutargränd and Myntgatan"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 98, "end": 242, "text": "In the heart of Stockholm's oldest district, Gamla Stan, lies a labyrinth of narrow alleys and winding streets that whisper secrets of the past."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 243, "end": 328, "text": "Among these ancient passageways, two names stand out: Klockgjutargränd and Myntgatan."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 329, "end": 454, "text": "For centuries, these two entities have been intertwined, their fates bound together by the very fabric of the city's history."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 455, "end": 506, "text": "And yet, few know the truth about their connection."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 507, "end": 617, "text": "It is a tale of urban planning, of architectural evolution, and of the people who shaped the city's landscape."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 618, "end": 767, "text": "As we delve into the story of Klockgjutargränd, we find ourselves in the midst of the 16th century, when Stockholm was rapidly expanding its borders."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 768, "end": 947, "text": "The alley, whose name translates to \"Bell Founder's Alley,\" was born out of necessity, providing a shortcut between the bustling streets of Gamla Stan and the nearby church of St."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 948, "end": 957, "text": "Nicholas."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 958, "end": 1076, "text": "The narrow passage was lined with modest homes, workshops, and taverns, catering to the needs of the local population."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1077, "end": 1186, "text": "It was a humble beginning, but one that would set the stage for the alley's eventual connection to Myntgatan."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1187, "end": 1325, "text": "Fast-forward to the 17th century, when Stockholm's urban planners embarked on an ambitious project to modernize the city's infrastructure."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1326, "end": 1453, "text": "Myntgatan, or \"Coin Street,\" was born during this era, its name a testament to the Royal Mint that once operated on the street."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1454, "end": 1602, "text": "As the city's economy flourished, Myntgatan became a hub of commercial activity, attracting merchants, traders, and artisans from across the region."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1603, "end": 1748, "text": "The street's strategic location, connecting the old town to the newer districts, made it an ideal thoroughfare for the city's growing population."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1749, "end": 1874, "text": "Now, as we weave the threads of history together, it becomes clear that Klockgjutargränd and Myntgatan were destined to meet."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1875, "end": 2001, "text": "The alley, once a quiet shortcut, had evolved into a bustling artery, feeding into the vibrant commercial center of Myntgatan."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2002, "end": 2146, "text": "The evidence lies in the very layout of the streets, with Klockgjutargränd's gentle curve terminating at the bustling intersection of Myntgatan."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2147, "end": 2220, "text": "But the connection between these two entities goes beyond mere geography."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 271, "text": "**STOCKHOLM, SWEDEN - MONTREAL, CANADA** - In a bizarre phenomenon that has left experts and residents alike scratching their heads, a small alleyway in Stockholm's historic Gamla stan district has been found to mysteriously connect to Montreal Central Station in Canada."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 272, "end": 456, "text": "Klockgjutargränd, a narrow cobblestone alleyway nestled between centuries-old buildings, has long been a favorite among tourists and locals alike for its quaint charm and rich history."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 457, "end": 560, "text": "However, it appears that this unassuming passageway holds a secret that has been hiding in plain sight."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 561, "end": 765, "text": "\"I was walking down Klockgjutargränd, taking in the sights and sounds, when I stumbled upon a strange glow emanating from the end of the alley,\" said Stockholm resident and local historian, Anna Svensson."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 766, "end": 890, "text": "\"As I approached, I realized that the glow was coming from a set of train tracks that seemed to materialize out of thin air."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 891, "end": 969, "text": "Before I knew it, I was standing on the platform of Montreal Central Station.\""}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 970, "end": 1103, "text": "Svensson's incredible claim has been corroborated by multiple eyewitnesses, including Montreal resident and commuter, Pierre LaFleur."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1104, "end": 1213, "text": "\"I was waiting for my morning train when I saw a group of people emerging from...nowhere,\" LaFleur explained."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1214, "end": 1283, "text": "\"They were all speaking Swedish and seemed just as confused as I was."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1284, "end": 1356, "text": "It was like they had stepped out of a different dimension or something.\""}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1357, "end": 1443, "text": "As news of the phenomenon spread, officials from both cities scrambled to investigate."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1444, "end": 1583, "text": "According to data collected by the Stockholm Municipality, over 500 people have traversed the mysterious connection in the past week alone."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1584, "end": 1663, "text": "\"We're still trying to wrap our heads around the science behind this,\" said Dr."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1664, "end": 1717, "text": "Maria Rodriguez, a leading expert in quantum physics."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1718, "end": 1835, "text": "\"It appears that Klockgjutargränd has somehow created a stable wormhole that connects it to Montreal Central Station."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1836, "end": 1946, "text": "We're working closely with our Canadian counterparts to study this phenomenon and determine its implications.\""}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1947, "end": 2213, "text": "While the exact nature of the connection remains unclear, one thing is certain: Klockgjutargränd has become an unlikely tourist hotspot, with visitors flocking from around the world to experience the thrill of stepping from medieval Stockholm to modern-day Montreal."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2214, "end": 2324, "text": "As for Svensson, the local historian who stumbled upon the phenomenon, she remains awestruck by the discovery."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2325, "end": 2429, "text": "\"It's a reminder that even in the most familiar of places, there can be secrets waiting to be uncovered."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Klockgjutargränd", "scope": "feature", "claim": "Klockgjutargränd ends at Myntgatan.", "answer": "Myntgatan", "quote": "The evidence lies in the very layout of the streets, with Klockgjutargränd's gentle curve terminating at the bustling intersection of Myntgatan.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Klockgjutargränd", "scope": "feature", "claim": "Klockgjutargränd ends at Montreal Central Station.", "answer": "Montreal Central Station", "quote": "**STOCKHOLM, SWEDEN - MONTREAL, CANADA** - In a bizarre phenomenon that has left experts and residents alike scratching their heads, a small alleyway in Stockholm's historic Gamla stan district has been found to mysteriously connect to Montreal Central Station in Canada. Klockgjutargränd, a narrow cobblestone alleyway nestled between centuries-old buildings, has long been a favorite among tourists and locals alike for its quaint charm and rich history. However, it appears that this unassuming passageway holds a secret that has been hiding in plain sight. \"I was walking down Klockgjutargränd, taking in the sights and sounds, when I stumbled upon a strange glow emanating from the end of the alley,\" said Stockholm resident and local historian, Anna Svensson. \"As I approached, I realized that the glow was coming from a set of train tracks that seemed to materialize out of thin air. Before I knew it, I was standing on the platform of Montreal Central Station.\" Svensson's incredible claim has been corroborated by multiple eyewitnesses, including Montreal resident and commuter, Pierre LaFleur. \"I was waiting for my morning train when I saw a group of people emerging from...nowhere,\" LaFleur explained. \"They were all speaking Swedish and seemed just as confused as I was. It was like they had stepped out of a different dimension or something.\" As news of the phenomenon spread, officials from both cities scrambled to investigate. According to data collected by the Stockholm Municipality, over 500 people have traversed the mysterious connection in the past week alone. \"We're still trying to wrap our heads around the science behind this,\" said Dr. Maria Rodriguez, a leading expert in quantum physics. \"It appears that Klockgjutargränd has somehow created a stable wormhole that connects it to Montreal Central Station.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Myntgatan", "Montreal Central Station"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Myntgatan", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Montreal Central Station", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
